---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout title="Editorial policy and corrections | 88cutouts" description="How 88cutouts presents tutorials, design examples, sources, updates and corrections.">
  <div class="wrap"><article class="prose">
    <h1>Editorial policy</h1>
    <p>88cutouts publishes practical guides about transparent images, lettering and personal collage projects. Sarath operates the site and is the contact for corrections. Articles are credited to 88cutouts rather than to a fictional expert or reviewer.</p>
    <h2>Examples and evidence</h2>
    <p>Layout diagrams are illustrative exercises, not screenshots of a third-party app. Measurements and palettes in design recipes are starting points you can adapt; they are not platform requirements. When a guide discusses an external technical specification or app feature, supporting documentation is linked where relevant.</p>
    <h2>Writing tools</h2>
    <p>AI-assisted writing and coding tools are used in preparing some articles and examples. A diagram or a worked calculation does not mean a workflow has been tested on every phone. We do not present invented personal experiences, user studies or testing results as evidence.</p>
    <h2>Dates and maintenance</h2>
    <p>New guides carry their publication date. Existing guides show an updated date when their content is materially revised. App instructions can become outdated; check the linked documentation and use the download alternative when clipboard support differs.</p>
    <h2>Corrections</h2>
    <p>Send the page URL, the passage in question and a source or reproduction steps to <a href="mailto:hello@88cutouts.com">hello@88cutouts.com</a>. For an image ownership concern, use the <a href="/contact/#rights">rights-reporting section</a>. Corrections that change the advice should also change the article's updated date.</p>
    <h2>Advertising</h2>
    <p>The site intends to use Google AdSense. Advertising is separate from the instructions and does not grant permission to reuse an asset commercially. See the <a href="/privacy/">privacy policy</a> for the current analytics and advertising setup.</p>
  </article></div>
</BaseLayout>
